Z||000000||brian43||05-25-2001||10:37 PM||||I'm planing on making a lambo kit, but really dont really have all the $ to lay down for the v8 small block kit and a v8 small block. So I want to buy a fiero with a 5-speed v6 and turbo charge it and what not, but I cant find any. I drove all the way down the Cinci today(about 1 hour 45mins from Columbus) to buy what the guy said was v6 5-speed for $1,100(which I thought was too much, but what the only one I could find) and when I got there it was only a 4 speed. So I was a little pissed. I called one of my friends and he said that they only made 5-speeds in 1988(don't know if this is true), but I cant find any 1988 5 speed v6s only 4 bangers. Do they make any 5 speed v6s? Thanks,<BR>brian||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||05-25-2001||11:01 PM|||| late 86,87 and 88 V6 cars all had fivespeeds. Fourspeed cars aren't that bad. Many people use 84 4cyl 4speeds.Most had 4.10 gears.<P>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||05-25-2001||11:01 PM||||All manual trans Fiero's from 86 1/2 to 88 are 5 speeds.<P>$1100 for a V6 5sp too much? That's about as low as it can get, and for that price it would probably be thrashed. A decent 88GT w/5sp goes for $5000 plus.<P>You seem to be new to Fieros. I suggest you read through the threads here. You need a little education<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||brian43||05-25-2001||11:23 PM||||Yes, I do need to do some more research on these cars. I always thought they were a joke b/c my friends uncle had one and it was the biggest pos ever it even had bullet holes. But really after driving that 4 speed it was not that bad of a car had good pick up. But I really dont want to put that much into a car that im only using the chasie. I might still get the v8 kit and drop a v8 in it, but how will a stock 5 speed trany hold up with a 350? Thanks,<BR>brian ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bcwawright||05-26-2001||12:13 AM||||If your doing a Lambo rebody you will be stretching the chasis 11" and that will allow you to put the motor inline with the chassis. You can then use a Porsche 930 or G50 transaxle......your choice of engines are just about unlimited as long as you can find an adapter plate. Ford's 4.9L OHC motor can put out some major hp if you want something exotic and you can go with the buick V6 turbo(Grand National)which you can get over 400hp and 400ftlbs of torque.Your choices are only limited by your budget. DR Replica Cars sells a chrome moly tube chasis for the Lambo and Held MotorSports sells an awesome engine cradle that has F1 rear suspension for the Fiero Chassis.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo Spyder F355<P>||||reg||14
